{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>And they shall make for themselves tzitzit.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, did not leave any matter in the world without giving Israel a commandment concerning it. One goes out to plow — <b>לא תחרוש בשור וחמור</b>. To sow — <b>לא תזרע כלאים</b>. To reap — <b>כי תקצור קצירך</b>. To knead — <b>ראשית עריסותכם</b>. Slaughtered and gave to the priest — <b>הזרוע והלחיים והקבה</b>. A bird's nest — <b>שלח תשלח</b>. In beast and bird — <b>ושפך את דמו וכסהו בעפר</b>. Planted — <b>וערלתם ערלתו</b>. She gave birth to a male — <b>ימול בשר ערלתו</b>. Burying the dead — <b>לא תתגודדו</b>. Shaving — <b>לא תקיפו</b>. Built a house — <b>ועשית מעקה</b>, and <b>וכתבתם על מזוזות</b>. Covered oneself in a garment — <b>ועשו להם ציצת</b>." "<b>On the tzitzit of the wing.</b> With the tzitzit of the wing, like the field of the earth — meaning, with the tzitzit of the wing which is white, they shall give <b>פתיל תכלת</b>. And so our Rabbis said."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:11.358358201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}